.TH COF-RUN 1 "2026-11-13" "cof 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cof-run \- Execute an orchestration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
cof run [OPTIONS] [orchestration]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Executes an orchestration document: a bundled name (cof list), a local path,
or (with --last) the most recently run orchestration's own saved arguments.
Config resolution runs first (CIRCUITRY_CONFIG, then a trusted project config,
then the global config), then the document's effects run in order.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B orchestration
ORCHESTRATION Path to orchestration file, or name of a bundled orchestration.
.TP
.B --config, -c
CONFIG Path to config JSON (or use CIRCUITRY_CONFIG).
.TP
.B --state, -s
STATE Optional input state JSON.
.TP
.B --out, -o
OUT Write resulting state JSON to this path.
.TP
.B --pretty
Pretty-print JSON when writing/printing.
.TP
.B --print
Print resulting state JSON to stdout.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Skip adapter calls; validate/plan only.
.TP
.B --json
Machine-readable output only (minimal logs).
.TP
.B --quiet
Suppress non-essential output.
.TP
.B --verbose, -v
Show detailed progress.
.TP
.B --live-state
LIVE_STATE Mirror state atomically to this file while the run goes (at most
every 0.5 s, and once more when it ends). For live monitoring.
.TP
.B --events
EVENTS Write a JSONL stream of effect starts and ends to this file as the run
goes (created or truncated up front). Shows what --live-state cannot: a
running tree branch, use child, or chain leaf.
.TP
.B -e
ENV_VARS Inline state variable (KEY=VALUE). Repeatable.
.TP
.B --label
LABEL Literal text for this run's label, shown wherever a run's label appears
(e.g. --events' run_start, runtime.last_run.label). Beats the document's own
top-level label: template; never rendered. Cleaned the same way either way:
whitespace collapsed to one space, control characters and escape sequences
dropped, trimmed, and cut at 64 characters; empty after cleaning means no
label. --resume re-renders the document's label from the same inputs unless
this is given.
.TP
.B --tail
Print only the final effect's value as plain text. Ideal for piping.
.TP
.B --last
Re-run the most recent orchestration with the same arguments.
.TP
.B --resume
RESUME Resume an interrupted or failed run of the SAME orchestration from its
saved state: 'last' (the most recent run's --out) or a run-id (looked up in
the orchestration's configured runtime.persistence backend). Effects whose
node already finished without error are skipped and reused; the first
unfinished or failed one, and everything after it, reruns. A named loop
resumes at its first unfinished pass. Combine with --state <file> to resume
from a specific saved state file directly instead of 'last'/a run-id.
.TP
.B --force
With --resume, continue even though the orchestration's content changed since
the saved run.
.TP
.B --skip-preflight
Bypass dependency preflight; run even if check()s reported missing deps.
.TP
.B --allow-capabilities
ALLOW_CAPABILITIES Comma-separated capabilities
(shell,python_eval,fs-write,network) to approve for this run without prompting
— a scripted/CI escape hatch for a use: ref: child that needs fresh consent.
Not persisted; see `cof trust` to approve a document permanently.
.TP
.B --profile
PROFILE Named profile to apply (profiles/<name>.yml, orchestration-scoped wins
over project-level). Precedence: CLI > profile > orchestration > config.
.TP
.B --profile-from-state
PROFILE_FROM_STATE Reconstruct and apply the profile recorded at
runtime.effective_settings.profile in this state JSON (e.g. a prior --out),
instead of discovering profiles/<name>.yml by name. Fails if that record was
redacted. Mutually exclusive with --profile.
.TP
.B --adapter
ADAPTER Adapter to use for this run. Beats CIRCUITRY_ADAPTER, --profile, and
the orchestration.
.TP
.B --model
MODEL Model to use for this run. Beats CIRCUITRY_MODEL, --profile, and the
orchestration.
.TP
.B --explain-routing
Print each prompt effect's complexity score, band, and model choice as it
dispatches. Needs runtime.complexity.scoring.enabled; prints nothing if
scoring is off. Suppressed by --quiet/--json.
.TP
.B --decompose-out
DECOMPOSE_OUT Write every triggered decomposition's generated orchestration to
this directory, one file per effect (failed plans included, marked as such).
Needs runtime.complexity.decomposition.enabled; a run that never decomposes
writes nothing.
.TP
.B --scoring, --no-scoring
Force runtime.complexity.scoring on/off for this run. Beats --profile and the
orchestration/config; omit to leave it resolved as configured.
.TP
.B --routing, --no-routing
Force runtime.complexity.routing on/off for this run. Beats --profile and the
orchestration/config; --no-routing also drops any profile per-effect routing
pin, since routing is off for the whole run either way. Requires scoring (from
this flag or config) when turned on.
.TP
.B --decompose, --no-decompose
Force runtime.complexity.decomposition on/off for this run. Beats --profile
and the orchestration/config. Requires scoring (from this flag or config) when
turned on.
.TP
.B --split, --no-split
Force runtime.complexity.splitting on/off for this run. Beats --profile and
the orchestration/config. Needs no scoring: an effect's own
split.budget_tokens still splits even with this off, and --no-split does not
stop it either — only an effect's own split.enabled: false opts it out.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B cof run hello-world
Runs a bundled orchestration by name.
.TP
.B cof run my-flow.yml -e name=world --out state.json
Runs a local document with one input, writing the final state to a file.
.TP
.B cof run --last
Re-runs the most recent orchestration with the same arguments, from
~/.config/circuitry/last-run.json.
.TP
.B cof run my-flow.yml --resume last
Resumes the most recent interrupted or failed run of the same orchestration
from its saved state.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_CONFIG
An explicit config JSON path. Checked before a trusted project config in the
current directory and the global config; replaces both rather than layering on
top of them.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_MODEL
Overrides the resolved config's default_model.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_ADAPTER
Overrides the resolved config's default_adapter.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_ADAPTER_URL
Overrides the resolved default adapter's own base_url.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_COMFYUI_URL
Overrides the comfyui plugin's own base_url.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_SYSTEMONE_URL
Overrides the systemone plugin's own base_url.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_ENABLED_ADAPTERS
Comma-separated allowlist, narrowing (never widening) the resolved config's
enabled_adapters.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_ENABLED_PLUGINS
Comma-separated allowlist, narrowing (never widening) the resolved config's
enabled_plugins.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_ENABLED_TOOLS
Comma-separated allowlist, narrowing (never widening) the resolved config's
enabled_tools.
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_ENVIRONMENT
Overrides the resolved config's environment (dev, prod, or test).
.TP
.B CIRCUITRY_TRUST_PROJECT_CONFIG
Trusts a project config in the current directory without running cof trust
first.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/circuitry/config.json
The global config, the last layer config resolution tries.
.TP
.I ~/.config/circuitry/.env
Private environment variables, loaded before config resolution (written by cof
setup).
.TP
.I ~/.config/circuitry/trusted.json
Project configs trusted by cof trust; config resolution consults it before
applying a discovered project config.
.TP
.I ./circuitry.config.json, ./config.json
A project config in the working directory, applied only once trusted.
.TP
.I ~/.config/circuitry/last-run.json
This run's own arguments, for a later --last or --resume last. Secret-looking
values are redacted before being written, and --last refuses to replay a
redacted run.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The run finished without error.
.TP
.B 1
The run failed, or the orchestration could not be found.
.TP
.B 2
A usage error -- an unrecognized option or missing argument.
.TP
.B 129
The run was interrupted by SIGHUP.
.TP
.B 130
The run was interrupted by SIGINT (Ctrl-C).
.TP
.B 143
The run was interrupted by SIGTERM.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBcof(1)\fR, \fBcof-validate(1)\fR, \fBcof-list(1)\fR, \fBelectricity-run(1)\fR
